#!/bin/sh
# A fake Codex CLI: same subcommands and JSONL stream, no network, no tokens. FAKE_SCENARIO
# picks the behavior. Every invocation appends its arguments and the billing-related
# environment to $CODEX_HOME/invocations, for assertions.
mkdir -p "$CODEX_HOME"
{
  printf 'ARGS %s\n' "$*"
  printf 'ENV OPENAI_API_KEY=[%s] CODEX_API_KEY=[%s]\n' "${OPENAI_API_KEY:-}" "${CODEX_API_KEY:-}"
} >> "$CODEX_HOME/invocations"

case "$1 $2" in
  "exec --help")
    if [ "$FAKE_SCENARIO" = old_cli ]; then echo "Usage: codex exec --json --disable"; else
      echo "Usage: codex exec --json --ignore-user-config --ignore-rules --disable --skip-git-repo-check"; fi
    exit 0 ;;
  "features list")
    if [ "$FAKE_SCENARIO" = no_feature ]; then echo "something stable true"; exit 0; fi
    printf 'shell_tool  stable  true\nunified_exec  stable  true\nbrowser_use  stable  true\nnew_tool  experimental  true\nitem_ids  removed  true\nmemories  stable  false\n'
    exit 0 ;;
  "debug models")
    echo '{"models":[{"slug":"gpt-fake","display_name":"GPT Fake","supported_reasoning_levels":[{"effort":"low"},{"effort":"high"}]}]}'
    exit 0 ;;
  "login status")
    case "$FAKE_SCENARIO" in
      logged_out) echo "Not logged in" >&2; exit 1 ;;
      api_key) echo "Logged in using an API key - sk-proj-***"; exit 0 ;;
      *) echo "Logged in using ChatGPT"; exit 0 ;;
    esac ;;
esac

prompt=$(cat)
session="fake-thread-1"
prev=""
for a in "$@"; do
  [ "$prev" = "resume" ] && case "$a" in -*) ;; *) session="$a" ;; esac
  [ "$a" = "resume" ] && prev="resume"
done
# The session ID is the argument right before the final "-".
if [ "$2" = "resume" ]; then
  n=$#; i=1
  for a in "$@"; do [ "$i" = "$((n - 1))" ] && session="$a"; i=$((i + 1)); done
fi
printf '{"type":"thread.started","thread_id":"%s"}\n' "$session"
printf '{"type":"turn.started"}\n'

case "$FAKE_SCENARIO" in
  rate_limit)
    printf '{"type":"error","message":"You have hit your usage limit. Try again later."}\n'
    printf '{"type":"turn.failed","error":{"message":"You have hit your usage limit."}}\n'
    exit 1 ;;
  expired)
    printf '{"type":"turn.failed","error":{"message":"401 Unauthorized: your refresh token has expired, please log in again"}}\n'
    exit 1 ;;
  gone)
    echo "Error: no rollout found for thread id $session" >&2
    exit 1 ;;
  crash)
    printf '{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"i0","type":"agent_message","text":"working"}}\n'
    echo "segfault" >&2
    exit 139 ;;
  no_result)
    exit 0 ;;
  ran_command)
    printf '{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"i0","type":"command_execution","command":"cat auth.json","status":"in_progress"}}\n' ;;
  hang)
    sleep 300 ;;
esac

printf '{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"i1","type":"file_change"}}\n'
printf 'this line is not JSON and must be tolerated\n'
printf '{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"i2","type":"reasoning","text":"secret thoughts"}}\n'
printf '{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"i3","type":"agent_message","text":"echo: %s"}}\n' "$prompt"
printf '{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1}}\n'
